<div style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.14; max-width: 1100px; margin: 0; color: #111;">
  <div style="border: 1px solid #c9c9c9; padding: 8px; margin: 0 0 6px 0; background: #f7f7f7;">
    <div style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 4px 0;">Student Guide: Same Unit Rate or Different Unit Rate?</div>
    <div style="margin: 0;">A unit rate tells the cost for <strong>1 item</strong>. To compare statements, find the unit rate for the original statement and for each row.</div>
  </div>
  <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; table-layout: fixed; margin: 0;">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 58%; vertical-align: top; padding: 0 6px 0 0;">
          <div style="border: 1px solid #c9c9c9; padding: 8px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 15pt; margin: 0 0 4px 0;">1. Big Idea</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 4px 0;">Two statements have the <strong>same unit rate</strong> if they have the same cost for 1 item.</div>
            <div style="margin: 0;">Use this idea:</div>
            <div style="margin: 4px 0 0 0; text-align: center;"><span style="color: #a85a00; font-weight: bold;">total cost</span> <span style="display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; margin: 0 6px;"> <span style="display: block; border-bottom: 1px solid #111; padding: 0 6px;">total cost</span> <span style="display: block; padding: 0 6px;">number of items</span> </span> = <span style="color: #1b7f3a; font-weight: bold;">cost for 1 item</span></div>
          </div>
          <br>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #c9c9c9; padding: 8px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 15pt; margin: 0 0 4px 0;">2. Step-by-Step Method</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 3px 0;"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Find the original unit rate.</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 3px 0;"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Find the row&rsquo;s unit rate.</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 3px 0;"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Compare the two unit rates.</div>
            <div style="margin: 0;"><strong>Step 4:</strong> If the cost for 1 item is the same, choose <strong>Same unit rate</strong>. If not, choose <strong>Different unit rate</strong>.</div>
          </div>
          <br>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #c9c9c9; padding: 8px; margin: 0 0 6px 0;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 15pt; margin: 0 0 4px 0;">Original Example</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 4px 0;"><strong>Statement:</strong> A customer bought <span style="color: #1167b1; font-weight: bold;">4 sandwiches</span> for <span style="color: #a85a00; font-weight: bold;">$24</span>.</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 4px 0;">Find the unit rate:</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 4px 0; text-align: center;"><span style="display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;"> <span style="display: block; border-bottom: 1px solid #111; padding: 0 8px;"><span style="color: #a85a00; font-weight: bold;">$24</span></span> <span style="display: block; padding: 0 8px;"><span style="color: #1167b1; font-weight: bold;">4 sandwiches</span></span> </span> = <span style="color: #1b7f3a; font-weight: bold;">$6 per sandwich</span></div>
            <div style="margin: 0;">Now every row must be compared to <span style="color: #1b7f3a; font-weight: bold;">$6 per item</span>.</div>
          </div>
          <br>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #c9c9c9; padding: 8px; margin: 0;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 15pt; margin: 0 0 4px 0;">3. Worked Examples</div>
            <br><br>
            <div style="border: 1px solid #d6d6d6; padding: 7px; margin: 0 0 6px 0; background: #fbfbfb;">
              <div style="font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 3px 0;">Example A: Same Unit Rate</div>
              <div style="margin: 0 0 3px 0;">12 tacos were sold for $72.</div>
              <div style="margin: 0 0 3px 0;"><span style="display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;"> <span style="display: block; border-bottom: 1px solid #111; padding: 0 8px;"><span style="color: #a85a00; font-weight: bold;">$72</span></span> <span style="display: block; padding: 0 8px;"><span style="color: #1167b1; font-weight: bold;">12 tacos</span></span> </span> = <span style="color: #1b7f3a; font-weight: bold;">$6 per taco</span></div>
              <div style="margin: 0;"><strong>Answer:</strong> Same unit rate, because $6 per item matches the original.</div>
            </div>
            <br>
            <div style="border: 1px solid #d6d6d6; padding: 7px; margin: 0 0 6px 0; background: #fbfbfb;">
              <div style="font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 3px 0;">Example B: Different Unit Rate</div>
              <div style="margin: 0 0 3px 0;">$50 was the total cost for 10 jars of jam.</div>
              <div style="margin: 0 0 3px 0;"><span style="display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;"> <span style="display: block; border-bottom: 1px solid #111; padding: 0 8px;"><span style="color: #a85a00; font-weight: bold;">$50</span></span> <span style="display: block; padding: 0 8px;"><span style="color: #1167b1; font-weight: bold;">10 jars</span></span> </span> = <span style="color: #1b7f3a; font-weight: bold;">$5 per jar</span></div>
              <div style="margin: 0;"><strong>Answer:</strong> Different unit rate, because $5 per item does not match $6 per item.</div>
            </div>
            <br><br>
            <div style="border: 1px solid #d6d6d6; padding: 7px; margin: 0; background: #fbfbfb;">
              <div style="font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 3px 0;">Example C: Different Unit Rate Even Though Both Numbers Changed</div>
              <div style="margin: 0 0 3px 0;">For $60, a customer bought 8 muffins.</div>
              <div style="margin: 0 0 3px 0;"><span style="display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;"> <span style="display: block; border-bottom: 1px solid #111; padding: 0 8px;"><span style="color: #a85a00; font-weight: bold;">$60</span></span> <span style="display: block; padding: 0 8px;"><span style="color: #1167b1; font-weight: bold;">8 muffins</span></span> </span> = <span style="color: #1b7f3a; font-weight: bold;">$7.50 per muffin</span></div>
              <div style="margin: 0;"><strong>Answer:</strong> Different unit rate. Both numbers changed, but the cost for 1 item changed too.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
