          <br>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #c9c9c9; padding: 8px; margin: 0 0 6px 0; background: #fff7f7;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 15pt; margin: 0 0 4px 0;">Common Mistakes</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 4px 0;"><strong>Mistake 1:</strong> Comparing only the total costs.</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 4px 0;">A higher total cost does not always mean a different unit rate.</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 4px 0;"><strong>Mistake 2:</strong> Comparing only the number of items.</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 4px 0;">More items can still have the same unit rate.</div>
            <div style="margin: 0 0 4px 0;"><strong>Mistake 3:</strong> Thinking both numbers changing means the rate stayed the same.</div>
            <div style="margin: 0;">The rate is the same only when the cost for 1 item is the same.</div>
